							<font size="6"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: violet; FONT-FAMILY: AuntJudy; mso-bidi-font-size: 24.0pt"> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 20pt; COLOR: violet; FONT-FAMILY: AuntJudy; mso-bidi-font-size: 24.0pt">Chansonette Lachat</span><span style="FONT-SIZE: 20pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Arial Unicode MS'; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /><o:p></o:p></span></p></span></font> <div class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: violet; FONT-FAMILY: AuntJudy; mso-bidi-font-size: 13.5pt"> <hr align="center" width="100%" size="2" /> </span></div> <p class="MsoBodyText" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: violet; FONT-FAMILY: AuntJudy; mso-bidi-font-size: 13.5pt">Chans or Chanson, a beautiful white tigress, was the eldest of a litter of four cute Vah Shir kits born into a well to do family in the lower nobility of Shar Vahl. She showed an early penchant for music and never really considered any other profession. She studied hard and has done well completing her citizenship quest and other tasks asked of her by her people. Her siblings include two brothers, Neko a tiger warrior, who disappeared at a young age and has not been seen since, and Thepilzbery, a white tiger like her, who is the family shaman as well as a skilled baker of pastries. Her sister Macavatiera, a black panther, is the black "cat" of the family having left home and chosen the life of a rogue at an early age. Nevertheless Chans and Macav are friends as well as sisters and get along together well.</span><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: violet; FONT-FAMILY: AuntJudy; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: violet; FONT-FAMILY: AuntJudy; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: violet; FONT-FAMILY: AuntJudy; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">One advantage of a well to do birth was that Chans never had to go through the trials of crafting her own armor, but had a nice set of introductory equipment and instrument given to her for her use. However since that time she has completed a number of quests to prove herself and better her equipment on her own.<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: violet; FONT-FAMILY: AuntJudy; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoBodyText2" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#ee82ee"><font face="AuntJudy">Not interested in the life of a harem singer for a noble husband Chans left home at a fairly young age to seek her fortune in the world as a wandering bard. She is a friendly and generally happy creature, although she can occasionally be moody. She often adventures and travels alone, however, she is most happy when in the company of others. Although never married or in a serious relationship she does spend time whenever she can, traveling with a Vah Shir Best Lord that she has known since birth.<o:p></o:p></font></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: violet; FONT-FAMILY: AuntJudy; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: violet; FONT-FAMILY: AuntJudy; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA">One day a wood elf druidess friend by the name of Xenawyr stopped her in the wilds of Norrath and invited her to join a young guild that had formed called Moonlight Redemption. This new guild with a friendly atmosphere appealed to her and she accepted the invitation that was given by the cleric guild leader Amyana whom she took an instant liking to. She was pleased when her sister Macavatiera chose to join the guild as well. She looks forward to new friends and new adventures in her days ahead in Norrath</span></p>
							
